    "title": "Behind Enemy Lines: Bob Chesney's most important UCLA staff hire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Matt Zemek ,\n12 hours ago HARRISONBURG, VIRGINIA - NOVEMBER 22: Bob Chesney Head Coach and Colin Hitschler Defense Coach of James Madison Dukes in action on the sidelines during a game against Washington State Cougars at Bridgeforth Stadium on November 22, 2025 in Harrisonburg, Virginia. (Photo by Brien Aho/Getty Images) By Brien Aho, Getty Images We continue our USC Behind Enemy Lines series with UCLA Wire editor Dylan McNeill. Next question: Who is Bob Chesney's most important staff hire going into the coach's first season with the Bruins ?\n\"The quickest way to start playing competitive football is having a strong defense, which makes new UCLA defensive coordinator Colin Hitschler the most important hire for Bob Chesney’s staff,\" McNeill told us. \"Hitschler has had co-defensive coordinator experience at Alabama, Wisconsin, Cincinnati and with Chesney at James Madison . Hitschler has coached some strong defenses over the past few years and if that can continue in 2026, UCLA has a shot at playing winning football in the Big Ten this season.\"\nIt's hard to argue with McNeill's answer. When UCLA was able to stand up to USC, it was because the Bruins had a physical, hard-nosed defense under then-coordinator D'Anton Lynn. When UCLA's defense was soft under other coordinators, the Bruins really didn't have a chance against the Trojans . Whether Colin Hitschler hits the mark as defensive coordinator is certainly a core variable for UCLA football this season. The Trojans hope he does as well as Alex Grinch did at USC. That would put the Men of Troy in position to run Los Angeles for many more years.\nContact/Follow @TrojansWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook to follow ongoing coverage of USC Trojans news, notes and opinion .\nThis article originally appeared on Trojans Wire: Behind Enemy Lines: Bob Chesney's most important UCLA staff hire",
    "summary": "12 hours ago HARRISONBURG, VIRGINIA - NOVEMBER 22: Bob Chesney Head Coach and Colin Hitschler Defense Coach of James Madison Dukes in action on the sidelines during a game against Washington State Cougars at Bridgeforth Stadium on November 22, 2025 in Harrisonburg, Virginia. Hitschler has coached some strong defenses over the past few years and if that can continue in 2026, UCLA has a shot at playing winning football in the Big Ten this season.\" Whether Colin Hitschler hits the mark as defensive coordinator is certainly a core variable for UCLA football this season.",
